# AnnPocketDb :: ci/tsan.supp
#
# ThreadSanitizer suppressions. This file should stay EMPTY (or very nearly
# so) for a project at AnnPocketDb's stage. A suppression here means "we've
# investigated this report and decided it's a false positive or an accepted,
# understood non-issue" -- not "this is annoying, make it go away."
#
# Do NOT add a suppression for anything touching:
#   - core/free_list.*
#   - core/page_manager.*
#   - core/reader_table.*
#   - btree/btree.cpp, btree/cursor.cpp
#   - txn/transaction.*
# A TSan report in any of these is exactly the class of bug this whole
# effort exists to catch. Suppressing one here defeats the purpose -- fix
# the race or, if it's genuinely a false positive, add a narrowly-scoped
# race:/deadlock: entry with a comment explaining precisely why it's benign
# (e.g. "the second access is provably ordered by X, TSan just can't see
# it through Y").
#
# Third-party code TSan sometimes flags spuriously (safe to suppress once
# confirmed against the upstream project's own TSan status):
#
# race:libc.so
# race:std::__1::__libcpp_atomic_refcount_increment

# (intentionally empty -- add entries above this line with a comment per
# entry explaining why, and a link/reference to the investigation)
